# System packages for a Heroku buildpack build (issue #347). Read by the
# heroku-community/apt buildpack, which has to be FIRST in the buildpack list:
# it downloads these into /app/.apt and exports PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH both
# to the buildpacks that run after it and to the dyno itself.
#
# Nothing here is read by the Coolify build. That one is railpack.json, which
# installs the Debian bookworm packages with apt-get.
#
# lua5.4 is the RUNTIME. The scripting sandbox spawns it as a child process on
# every message and lib/rubotty/scripting/child.rb finds it by walking PATH for
# the name. No Heroku stack preinstalls Lua, so without this line the whole
# scripting feature reports itself uninstalled.
#
# MessagePack is the one rock the sandbox requires, and there is no line for
# it here: noble's luarocks still links against Lua 5.1 and cannot install
# into a 5.4 tree, and unlike dkjson before it, Ubuntu packages no
# lua-messagepack either. vendor/lua/MessagePack.lua is the fix, a pure Lua
# file checked into this repository rather than fetched by anything at build
# time; .profile points LUA_PATH at it.
#
# The other three dialect transpilers (fennel, moonc, tl) are deliberately
# absent. Nothing packages them for Ubuntu and luarocks cannot reach Lua 5.4
# here, so a Heroku deploy offers plain Lua and reports MoonScript, Fennel and
# Teal unavailable. That is an ordinary state the dashboard already handles: a
# dialect with no compiler is simply not offered. The Coolify build has all
# four.
#
# lua5.4 lives in Ubuntu's universe component. If a build fails with "Unable to
# locate package lua5.4", the stack image's sources do not carry universe, and
# the fix is a line like the one below, which this buildpack APPENDS to the
# stack's own sources rather than replacing them. Match the mirror to the dyno
# architecture: archive.ubuntu.com serves amd64, ports.ubuntu.com serves arm64.
#
#   :repo:deb http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu noble main universe
#
# imagemagick supplies the `convert` binary Util::ImageShrinker spawns to bring
# an oversized picture under a platform's upload limit (issue #642), and ffmpeg
# supplies the ffmpeg and ffprobe pair Util::VideoTranscoder will use for the
# same job on a video. Both are found by walking PATH for the name, so a stack
# without them simply reports the shrink strategies unavailable at boot and
# file_rehosting links the file instead.
lua5.4
imagemagick
ffmpeg
